WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Speaker 1: Sarah Palin is running for a House&nbsp;
of Representatives seat representing Alaska.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:10.200
She's the former mayor of Wasilla, the former&nbsp;
partial term governor of Alaska and former vice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:16.080
presidential running mate back in 2008. You might&nbsp;
remember she quit being governor before the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.960
her term and she is essentially giving up. And&nbsp;
if I didn't think she was such a disaster for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:27.300
the country, I might feel a little bit bad for&nbsp;
her, but I don't. Sarah Palin appeared on Steve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:33.480
Bannon's The War Room, and she said there, you&nbsp;
know what, I'm no longer accepting donations. I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.360
gotten rid of my campaign staff, staff because&nbsp;
they gave me bad advice. Let me interpret this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.880
for you. Sarah Palin has given up. She's trying to&nbsp;
save money because it would be pointless to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.160
spending money because she's obviously going to&nbsp;
lose. But look at the spin. I didn't know what way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.180
was up and down after I heard this the first time.
Speaker 3: I'm going to get in trouble for saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.800
this. But sometimes you wonder the people who&nbsp;
are actually advising, working on campaigns.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.060
You got to wonder if they're really in it for&nbsp;
the right reasons, because sometimes they give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:08.640
really crappy advice and effort. So I'm doing a&nbsp;
lot of this myself. I'm not going to ask people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:14.280
for donations, though, which ticks off those in&nbsp;
my campaign who and other campaigns, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.540
because they look at this as a business and&nbsp;
they get a cut of funds raised. I don't ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.700
people for money because I've won all the races&nbsp;
that I've been in over my life except one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:30.351
the big one, and I've done it being outspent&nbsp;
10 to 1 or whatever it is, because, you know.&nbsp;

00:01:30.351 --> 00:01:34.680
Speaker 1: She'll be outspent 10 to 0.
Speaker 3: Now, our role and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.240
it's always worked well.
Speaker 1: Yeah. And you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:45.960
tell from the look on Steve Bannon's face, it's&nbsp;
over for Sarah Palin. What this means is nobody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:52.920
is supporting me anymore. I'm out of money. No&nbsp;
one's donating anyway. So I'll say I'm no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.920 --> 00:02:00.360
accepting donations, as we talked about last week.&nbsp;
Republican Alaska Senator Lisa murkowski is voting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:06.360
for Sarah Palin's Democratic opponent. People&nbsp;
don't like that Sarah Palin quit being governor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:13.320
A lot of Republicans in Alaska don't like Sarah&nbsp;
Palin. And this is just the last nail in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:18.840
coffin. I'm no longer having any staff and I'm&nbsp;
no longer accepting donations. You're giving up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.860
Sarah. You're giving up. And my hope is&nbsp;
and I don't know if this will be the case.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:29.580
My hope is that this will really be the end&nbsp;
of Sarah Palin's political career, a career&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:35.940
that never really should have gotten started.&nbsp;
But it did. And she is really in a in a sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:43.320
